>> title: Beef Rendang
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, coconut, indonesian, chiles, stew
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: rendang, rendang daging, dry beef curry
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the sauce goes from wet to dry to caught on the bottom, and past that it is bitter coconut through every piece

Blend @shallots{8}, @garlic{6%cloves}, @fresh ginger{2%in}(50 g), @galangal{2%in}(50 g), @ground turmeric{2%tsp}, @dried red chiles{10}(soaked in hot water) to a paste.

Fry @&(~1)spice paste{}, @coconut oil{3%Tbs} in a heavy #pot{}.

>> step: simmer uncovered 2 hr
Simmer @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in cubes), @coconut milk{40%oz}(1.2 L; three cans), @lemongrass{2%stalks}(bruised), @kaffir lime leaves{6} with @&(~1)fried paste{} for ~{2%hr}.

Season @&(~1)curry{} with @palm sugar{1%Tbs}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

>> step: toast and pound to kerisik
Toast @unsweetened grated coconut{1%cup}(85 g) in a dry #skillet{} until deep brown, then pound to a coarse kerisik.

>> step: reduce 1 hr until dark and dry
Reduce @&(~2)rendang{} with @&(~1)kerisik{} until the oil separates and the sauce clings, ~{60%min}.
